<title>PHILIPPINES: Philippines temporarily halts peso-dlr trades.</title>
<headline>Philippines temporarily halts peso-dlr trades.</headline>
<dateline>MANILA 1997-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bankers Association of the Philppines (BAP) has temporarily halted peso-dollar trades, an Allied Bank official said.</p>
<p>The Allied Bank's Dan Lorenzo, who is officer-in-charge for the day for the BAP peso-dollar trades, said the volatility band was breached. Under rules of the association, trades should be halted when the peso moves beyond 1 1/2 percent.</p>
<p>He said 26.40 was the reference rate used and the band was breached at 26.796.  </p>
<p>-- Manila newsroom (63 2) 841-8937</p>
</text>
